WEBVTT

00:02.730 --> 00:03.690
<b>Investigation Division 1</b>

00:03.690 --> 00:05.190
A joint investigation?
<b>Investigation Division 1</b>

00:05.190 --> 00:05.200
A joint investigation?

00:05.200 --> 00:08.410
One of the serial murders
causing a stir in Aichi Prefecture

00:08.410 --> 00:09.910
apparently happened here.

00:10.340 --> 00:12.120
Eagle Eye Kawasemi is coming.

00:12.120 --> 00:14.080
Eagle Eye Kawasemi?!

00:14.420 --> 00:16.940
With the top serial murder
clearance rate in the country?

00:16.940 --> 00:18.630
The super-skilled detective?

00:18.630 --> 00:21.790
The guy they say might become
superintendent general in his twenties?

00:21.790 --> 00:23.500
<i>The</i> Kawasemi Omito?!

00:26.010 --> 00:26.210
<b>Aim to be police
superintendent general!</b>

00:26.210 --> 00:27.820
Oh crap! That's right!
<b>Aim to be police
superintendent general!</b>

00:27.820 --> 00:31.260
Amamiya-senpai is also gunning
to be superintendent general!
<b>Aim to be police
superintendent general!</b>

00:31.880 --> 00:34.220
The detective overseeing
the joint operation...

00:34.220 --> 00:35.940
will be you, Isshiki.

00:35.940 --> 00:37.480
What? Me?

00:37.480 --> 00:40.710
Like I'd ever lend Kawasemi
any of my best men!

00:40.710 --> 00:42.690
That was backhandedly brutal!

00:47.560 --> 00:48.710
He's here.

00:48.710 --> 00:49.450
Huh?

00:59.750 --> 01:01.460
Your button is about to fall off!

01:02.170 --> 01:03.380
Trim your nails!

01:04.090 --> 01:05.800
Your necktie is sloppy!

01:06.470 --> 01:08.130
Your glasses are covered in fingerprints!

01:08.130 --> 01:10.220
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!
You missed spots shaving!

01:17.000 --> 01:18.430
Chaos...

01:19.360 --> 01:20.860
is the enemy of our work.

01:21.390 --> 01:23.110
He's terrifyingly impressive.

01:23.110 --> 01:25.620
Not one drop of water
gets past his eagle-eyed checks.

01:25.620 --> 01:28.360
He uses those tweezers
as deftly as threading a needle.

01:28.360 --> 01:30.940
And because he orders
his superiors around the same way,

01:30.940 --> 01:34.070
he's hard to peg for abuse of power.
An unusual sort of scum.

01:34.410 --> 01:37.590
Senpai, do you know Kawasemi-san personally?

01:37.590 --> 01:40.540
When I was a newbie, we were
at the same small, local station.

01:40.540 --> 01:42.750
Our paths split after that, though.

01:47.940 --> 01:50.040
I despise anything pointless.

01:50.040 --> 01:52.580
My many years of experience are telling me

01:52.580 --> 01:54.430
something I'll share quite frankly.

01:54.430 --> 01:58.010
I-I'm about to get the eagle-eyed check!

01:58.850 --> 02:01.390
You are so unsuited to be
a detective that it's tragic.

02:01.390 --> 02:02.540
Zero aptitude.

02:02.540 --> 02:04.370
Is that like "zero sugar"?

02:17.220 --> 02:20.540
<i>Forbidden
</i>Deductions
Ron    Kamonohashi's

03:37.570 --> 03:40.740
<b>#05   The Case of the Hand Collector</b>

03:43.910 --> 03:46.160
You seem well, Amamiya.

03:47.390 --> 03:48.620
You have some dust on your shoulder.

03:51.450 --> 03:52.920
Just try touching me, scum.

03:53.340 --> 03:54.760
I'll slit your throat.

03:56.720 --> 03:58.760
What's with this atmosphere?

04:00.030 --> 04:01.600
You haven't changed at all.

04:04.140 --> 04:05.280
Yamane.

04:05.280 --> 04:06.430
Sir?

04:06.430 --> 04:07.850
How long have you been there?

04:07.850 --> 04:09.820
A fresh set of tweezers for you.

04:09.820 --> 04:12.090
And with regards to the case,

04:12.090 --> 04:15.210
I've compiled files on similar
cases from all over.

04:15.590 --> 04:17.700
The red are local to the city,
the blue are domestic,

04:17.700 --> 04:19.660
and the yellow are from overseas.

04:20.160 --> 04:21.370
Your partner?

04:21.370 --> 04:25.090
Yes. I am the greatest detective in history,
and he is my right-hand man.

04:25.510 --> 04:30.330
Oh, hardly. I'm just glad to get
to work with you, Kawasemi-san.

04:30.330 --> 04:34.200
So he's able to please
the incredibly exacting Kawasemi-san?

04:34.200 --> 04:35.300
That's amazing.

04:36.580 --> 04:37.860
Kawasemi.

04:37.860 --> 04:40.690
I'll lend you the man who
caught your eagle eye for this job,

04:40.690 --> 04:42.710
Isshiki Totomaru here.

04:42.710 --> 04:44.220
H-Hello.

04:44.220 --> 04:45.960
Are you doing this to spite me?

04:45.960 --> 04:48.100
I'd call it making a snide remark.

04:48.100 --> 04:49.690
This is a living hell.

04:50.580 --> 04:51.650
How strange.

04:52.220 --> 04:53.840
I can't even see him.

04:53.840 --> 04:55.740
He's erased my very existence?!

04:56.180 --> 04:57.470
We're off to the scene, Yamane.

04:57.470 --> 04:58.470
Yes, sir.

04:58.470 --> 05:01.030
I've bought a bento you can eat in the car.

05:01.030 --> 05:02.450
U-Um...

05:02.450 --> 05:05.440
Do you now understand what a kind boss I am?

05:05.440 --> 05:08.220
I really do! You actually see me!

05:11.920 --> 05:12.730
Tokyo Central Art Museum

05:12.730 --> 05:14.380
What's the situation, Yamane?
Tokyo Central Art Museum

05:14.380 --> 05:14.710
Tokyo Central Art Museum

05:14.710 --> 05:18.190
The truck belongs to a company
from Aichi Prefecture, sir.

05:18.190 --> 05:22.430
The driver was told the cargo
was works of art such as statues.

05:23.020 --> 05:27.230
And one of the statues turned out
to be a dead body, is that right?

05:27.230 --> 05:28.100
A dead body?

05:32.730 --> 05:33.480
His...

05:34.030 --> 05:35.440
His hands are gone!

05:35.720 --> 05:38.240
Who would kill in such a cruel manner?

05:38.240 --> 05:39.620
So it's the same MO?

05:39.620 --> 05:41.530
Huh? By "the same," you mean...

05:42.120 --> 05:43.900
Let's investigate the body, Yamane.

05:43.900 --> 05:45.850
Right, he can't see me!

05:46.410 --> 05:51.370
I mean, to Eagle Eye Kawasemi,
I'm probably nothing more than a hindrance...

05:51.370 --> 05:53.340
But after seeing such a grisly corpse,

05:53.340 --> 05:55.830
I can't stand silently by and just watch!

05:55.830 --> 05:57.940
Except... what am I supposed to do?

05:57.940 --> 05:59.410
You called, Toto?

06:01.510 --> 06:02.420
It's me!

06:02.420 --> 06:03.470
Who are you?!

06:04.220 --> 06:05.760
Someone with "Kamo" in his name?

06:05.760 --> 06:08.480
Yes! I've come to save you.

06:08.480 --> 06:10.180
No one asked for your help.

06:10.180 --> 06:12.050
But you're at a loss, aren't you?

06:12.050 --> 06:15.150
Your lips flap when you think to yourself,
so you're easy to read.

06:16.590 --> 06:19.320
Hey there! Haven't seen your face
around here before.

06:21.030 --> 06:25.040
I am a consultant in all matters
involving hands.

06:28.120 --> 06:31.480
I am the hand puppet master,
Tekemono Kamomi!

06:31.480 --> 06:33.310
A crazy bomb just went off!

06:35.540 --> 06:35.970
Tekemono Kamomi
Consultant in All Things Hands

06:35.970 --> 06:37.500
A consultant?
Tekemono Kamomi
Consultant in All Things Hands

06:37.500 --> 06:37.510
A consultant?

06:37.510 --> 06:40.460
Did Amamiya arrange this? How unnecessary.

06:40.460 --> 06:44.320
I cannot have this investigation
hindered by some lackluster civilian.

06:44.320 --> 06:45.680
Kindly take your leave.

06:45.680 --> 06:48.890
Don't worry. I'm not lackluster, you see.

06:49.810 --> 06:50.850
Is that so?

06:50.850 --> 06:54.310
You look like you have something to say.
Please, by all means.

06:58.270 --> 07:01.450
A platypus's bill is commonly thought
to be hard like a bird's beak,

07:01.450 --> 07:04.030
but it's actually soft like rubber!

07:04.490 --> 07:05.780
Ow!

07:08.110 --> 07:09.700
Th-The feel of rubber!

07:09.700 --> 07:13.040
I insisted on it, of course.
It's a charming feature of the platypus.

07:15.930 --> 07:19.190
I will allow you to accompany me,
but do not get in the way.

07:19.190 --> 07:21.060
Was that a hint of acknowledgment?

07:21.060 --> 07:23.880
That detective is quite outstanding.

07:23.880 --> 07:25.770
He's absolutely incredible!

07:25.770 --> 07:28.590
He has the top serial murder
clearance rate in the nation.

07:28.590 --> 07:32.600
People call him Eagle Eye Kawasemi because
he sees through everything in an instant!

07:32.600 --> 07:34.310
Wh-What?

07:35.350 --> 07:38.720
That tweezer-wielding bastard!

07:38.720 --> 07:40.020
His poor face!

07:40.400 --> 07:41.860
He's not beating me!

07:41.860 --> 07:45.230
Toto, no matter what,
we're catching the culprit first!

07:45.230 --> 07:48.220
Sorry to rain on your parade,
but that's not happening.

07:48.220 --> 07:51.330
Thing is, Kawasemi-san's not
letting me in on anything.

07:51.330 --> 07:52.150
Not a problem.

07:52.150 --> 07:52.950
What?

07:53.910 --> 07:56.030
I have something that belongs
to Kawasemi-kun.

07:56.030 --> 07:57.620
That's Yamane-san!

07:58.150 --> 08:01.590
If you'd just asked, I would have told you.

08:02.340 --> 08:08.190
This case follows the same MO
as three other murders in Aichi Prefecture.

08:08.550 --> 08:12.240
The perpetrator kills his victims
with a single stab to the heart.

08:12.240 --> 08:16.520
And then, for some reason, he severs
their hands and takes them with him.

08:17.240 --> 08:18.730
How creepy.

08:19.060 --> 08:22.390
Because of his bizarre MO,
we've been calling him...

08:22.390 --> 08:23.690
the Hand Collector.

08:23.690 --> 08:24.940
The Hand Collector!

08:24.940 --> 08:26.090
What a cool name!

08:26.090 --> 08:27.400
I'm shocked how annoying that is.

08:28.230 --> 08:32.870
An unusual killer that even
Eagle Eye Kawasemi can't capture...

08:32.870 --> 08:34.940
The Hand Collector, huh?

08:34.940 --> 08:37.090
How terrifying.
It could turn you pale with fright.

08:37.090 --> 08:39.580
Don't say that while you
look pleased as punch!

08:39.580 --> 08:41.780
Kawasemi-san is amazing.

08:41.780 --> 08:45.500
He narrowed the list down
to just a few suspects.

08:46.690 --> 08:50.960
Then, last night, while informally
questioning one of them,

08:50.960 --> 08:53.990
we realized he had nothing
to refute our suspicions.

08:55.070 --> 08:58.100
That man has to be the Hand Collector.

08:58.100 --> 08:59.320
Wow!

08:59.320 --> 09:00.540
But...

09:03.830 --> 09:08.970
he put up a huge fight and fled
into an abandoned factory.

09:09.890 --> 09:13.100
There were only two ways
in and out of the building.

09:13.100 --> 09:18.000
Kawasemi-san and I split up to try
to catch him in a pincer maneuver.

09:18.000 --> 09:23.460
I found the culprit first. I was able
to subdue and handcuff him, but...

09:25.920 --> 09:28.560
He managed to shake Yamane off.

09:29.380 --> 09:31.870
I rushed there, and the culprit
came barreling at me.

09:31.870 --> 09:35.610
Though it's unthinkable, I let him escape.

09:36.310 --> 09:41.020
That is why I must be
the one to close this case.

09:43.060 --> 09:46.020
B-But if you know what
the culprit looks like,

09:46.020 --> 09:47.880
it won't be long before
you apprehend him, right?

09:47.880 --> 09:48.990
About that...

09:49.520 --> 09:51.140
I don't know how,

09:51.140 --> 09:55.450
but the man we believed to be
the Hand Collector last night...

09:56.480 --> 09:59.410
is now the handless corpse
sitting before you.

09:59.410 --> 10:00.250
What?

10:04.960 --> 10:06.960
Tokyo Central Art Museum

10:09.910 --> 10:13.180
The victim was the Hand Collector?

10:13.180 --> 10:15.950
In other words, the real Hand Collector

10:15.950 --> 10:17.640
is still out there somewhere.

10:18.850 --> 10:20.260
Hey!

10:21.520 --> 10:23.020
Excuse me.

10:24.730 --> 10:27.380
You're dressed lightly for this time of year.

10:27.380 --> 10:29.830
So you were killed in a heated room.

10:29.830 --> 10:31.440
Or you're a half-hearted exhibitionist.

10:31.440 --> 10:33.030
Of course he's not!

10:33.320 --> 10:34.150
What's this?

10:34.150 --> 10:35.860
This tattoo...

10:35.860 --> 10:37.210
A tree branch?

10:37.840 --> 10:40.080
No. This is...

10:40.080 --> 10:42.020
Oh, I know! It's kelp!

10:42.020 --> 10:43.160
It's a bird.

10:44.010 --> 10:47.030
I remember seeing it when I handcuffed him.

10:47.030 --> 10:49.460
That's definitely the guy from last night.

10:50.830 --> 10:52.240
I see.

10:54.420 --> 10:56.680
Well, this is a problem!

10:56.680 --> 10:57.400
What is it?

10:57.400 --> 10:59.190
I can't get these puppets off!

10:59.190 --> 11:00.350
Can we stay on track?!

11:00.350 --> 11:03.500
Dear, dear. It seems this was a huge waste.

11:04.350 --> 11:07.270
I don't have the time to play
with you. Go home.

11:07.270 --> 11:09.730
Kawasemi-kun, I'm disappointed in you!

11:09.730 --> 11:11.760
You're the one getting told to go home!

11:15.280 --> 11:18.090
What did you even come here for?

11:18.090 --> 11:19.870
Can't you pull any harder?

11:19.870 --> 11:21.570
Shut up!

11:29.710 --> 11:31.370
Ow, ow, ow...

11:31.370 --> 11:33.070
I'm so sorry!

11:35.880 --> 11:37.840
Can't you behave properly?

11:37.840 --> 11:39.300
Y-Yes, sir.

11:39.300 --> 11:42.760
Impressive, Detective Isshiki!
It's just as you deduced.

11:42.760 --> 11:43.850
What?

11:43.850 --> 11:45.850
That's made everything clear.

11:45.850 --> 11:48.310
Kawasemi-kun is lying.

11:49.580 --> 11:51.270
I'll say just one thing.

11:51.270 --> 11:55.740
It won't be Eagle Eye Kawasemi
who catches the Hand Collector.

11:56.100 --> 11:59.200
It'll be the pure, naïve fool,
Detective Isshiki!

12:00.000 --> 12:02.580
You think I'm lying, do you?

12:02.580 --> 12:03.760
On what grounds?

12:03.760 --> 12:05.660
Huh? Well...

12:05.660 --> 12:10.630
Kawasemi-kun, you easily dodged
Detective Isshiki charging at you just now.

12:10.630 --> 12:14.350
With such exceptional reflexes
and physical agility,

12:14.350 --> 12:19.400
there's no way a handcuffed culprit
would ever get past you.

12:21.380 --> 12:24.510
Then you rushed at me on purpose just now?

12:24.970 --> 12:27.780
I've heard one of Amamiya's new subordinates

12:27.780 --> 12:30.590
has been brilliantly cracking cases lately.

12:31.130 --> 12:32.610
I don't suppose...

12:34.690 --> 12:37.190
So you admit you lied, correct?

12:40.920 --> 12:41.920
Yes.

12:43.360 --> 12:46.700
Yamane handcuffed the culprit
and allowed him to get away.

12:47.370 --> 12:49.270
I wasn't present for it.

12:50.230 --> 12:53.810
I was watching the factory's
other exit, you see?

12:53.810 --> 12:55.340
Why the lie?

12:55.340 --> 12:59.550
That day, Yamane was missing
a button on his sleeve.

12:59.550 --> 13:00.680
Huh?

13:01.760 --> 13:03.950
I knew immediately from his expression.

13:04.470 --> 13:06.690
Though Yamane is an outstanding subordinate,

13:06.690 --> 13:10.050
these grotesque serial murders
have unnerved him.

13:10.690 --> 13:14.760
And as I could have predicted,
Yamane made a mistake in the final play.

13:16.110 --> 13:19.820
But I was aware of my
subordinate's mental state

13:19.820 --> 13:23.110
and failed to give him appropriate
guidance. It was on me.

13:23.110 --> 13:27.580
So you covered for him
and said you let the culprit get away.

13:28.330 --> 13:32.540
I thought he was cold,
but he cares about his assistant.

13:32.540 --> 13:35.250
I'm sorry! This is all my fault!

13:35.730 --> 13:38.210
I even made Kawasemi-san lie for me!

13:39.970 --> 13:41.930
What's this, Yamane-kyun?

13:41.930 --> 13:44.890
You're missing a button on your sleeve again.

13:44.890 --> 13:45.750
What?

13:47.810 --> 13:49.770
It can't be! I-It's gone!

13:51.240 --> 13:52.490
Yamane.

13:52.490 --> 13:53.990
I'll find it immediately!

13:53.990 --> 13:56.900
It must've come off
when Isshiki-san ran into me...

13:56.900 --> 13:59.110
Where is it? Where is it?!

13:59.650 --> 14:01.150
It's over here.

14:03.320 --> 14:05.070
It's perfect for a new eye!

14:05.070 --> 14:07.530
Hey! Don't upcycle it without permission!

14:09.850 --> 14:11.250
I'm so glad.

14:11.940 --> 14:13.820
I found it this time....

14:18.500 --> 14:20.340
Thank you for saying that.

14:20.340 --> 14:21.130
Huh?

14:21.780 --> 14:23.460
We only realize what's most important

14:25.500 --> 14:28.180
after it's gone.

14:28.180 --> 14:29.390
What?

14:33.060 --> 14:34.620
All right, take it away.

14:35.060 --> 14:36.020
Okay.

14:36.770 --> 14:37.310
Speaker

14:37.310 --> 14:39.020
How've you been, Tototo?
Speaker

14:39.020 --> 14:41.690
Wait, "Tototo"? Where've I heard that before?

14:41.690 --> 14:44.950
<b>Speaker
Hint: It's your new best friend!</b>

14:44.950 --> 14:45.660
<b>Speaker</b>

14:46.500 --> 14:48.790
That laugh! You're the tracking—

14:49.370 --> 14:50.830
Spitz?

14:50.830 --> 14:52.450
B-B-Bingo!

14:52.450 --> 14:54.160
I've looked into all kinds of stuff.

14:54.160 --> 14:57.020
The body in the truck is Mushanokouji Minoru.

14:57.020 --> 14:58.880
Perpetual part-timer. Forty-eight years old.

14:59.660 --> 15:02.120
I'm at his place right now...

15:03.420 --> 15:05.760
and it's absolutely unreal.

15:05.760 --> 15:06.150
<b>Hands</b>

15:06.150 --> 15:07.970
If there were a world competition
for hand obsession,
<b>Hands</b>

15:07.970 --> 15:08.860
<b>Hands
If there were a world competition
for hand obsession,</b>

15:08.860 --> 15:10.180
he'd represent Japan and be
guaranteed a top place.
<b>Hands</b>

15:10.180 --> 15:12.190
<b>Hand Heaven
he'd represent Japan and be
guaranteed a top place.</b>

15:12.190 --> 15:12.890
<b>Hand Heaven</b>

15:13.570 --> 15:17.350
His precious collection
is nicely refrigerated here, too.

15:19.780 --> 15:22.170
Three people's worth of hands.

15:23.530 --> 15:27.990
The man in the truck, Mushanokouji,
is definitely the Hand Collector.

15:28.290 --> 15:30.450
Thanks. That was a great help.

15:30.450 --> 15:32.030
What was all that?

15:32.030 --> 15:33.950
Er, uh...

15:35.170 --> 15:38.830
What's all this sticky stuff?
B-Black sugar syrup?

15:38.830 --> 15:40.580
Sorry. It went off by accident.

15:40.580 --> 15:41.620
Let's go wash it off.

15:41.620 --> 15:43.550
Why would you even need that function?!

15:43.550 --> 15:44.100
Seriously! I'm all sticky now.

15:44.100 --> 15:46.010
Come on, let's go.
Seriously! I'm all sticky now.

15:46.010 --> 15:46.890
Seriously! I'm all sticky now.

15:47.890 --> 15:49.970
Oh, Kawasemi-kun?

15:51.180 --> 15:54.880
When we get back,
Detective Isshiki says he'll solve the case.

15:54.880 --> 15:56.500
So just you wait, okay?

15:58.320 --> 16:00.360
He'll solve it?

16:22.110 --> 16:24.250
I hear you're going to solve the case.

16:24.250 --> 16:28.610
Very well. I'll humor the nonsensical
ramblings of a rookie detective.

16:28.610 --> 16:29.720
Okay.

16:29.720 --> 16:33.070
As the information you just received
from the Aichi police confirms,

16:33.070 --> 16:37.610
Mushanokouji is without a doubt
the Hand Collector serial killer.

16:39.670 --> 16:40.900
Yes, he is.

16:41.230 --> 16:42.550
Hold on!

16:42.550 --> 16:45.860
Mushanokouji's hands were taken too, right?

16:47.550 --> 16:51.630
Meaning that was done to make us think
there's another Hand Collector.

16:51.630 --> 16:53.830
It's the work of a copycat.

16:53.830 --> 16:55.830
That's rather obvious.

16:55.830 --> 16:57.310
The real question is,

16:57.310 --> 17:00.590
why would they go to the trouble
to imitate such a brutal murder?

17:01.060 --> 17:03.470
Actually, they didn't murder anyone.

17:04.710 --> 17:06.000
Mushanokouji...

17:06.770 --> 17:08.450
killed himself.

17:08.840 --> 17:09.660
What?

17:12.070 --> 17:15.090
Mushanokouji stabbed himself in the heart,

17:15.090 --> 17:17.690
splattering blood on his jacket sleeves.

17:18.110 --> 17:20.750
In order to make his death look like a murder,

17:20.750 --> 17:23.640
someone removed and hid his jacket.

17:23.640 --> 17:26.320
You mean to say that's why
he's dressed so lightly.

17:26.320 --> 17:28.320
Still, why would he kill himself?

17:28.730 --> 17:30.520
Once he was cornered by you two,

17:30.520 --> 17:33.780
the serial killer had no choice
but to accept his fate.

17:35.480 --> 17:40.000
If that's true, he took his life
in that abandoned factory.

17:40.450 --> 17:44.210
But we and Mushanokouji
were the only people there.

17:45.700 --> 17:49.670
It can't be. That means the person who
took Mushanokouji's hands was...

17:49.670 --> 17:51.290
That's right.

17:51.290 --> 17:55.520
It was the first person to find
Mushanokouji after he killed himself.

17:58.080 --> 18:00.350
Yamane-san, that would be you!

18:00.700 --> 18:01.790
Wha?!

18:01.790 --> 18:04.590
I-It couldn't possibly be me!

18:05.480 --> 18:08.690
You cornered Mushanokouji
in the abandoned factory at night.

18:09.310 --> 18:10.940
I'm sure it was pitch black in there.

18:11.680 --> 18:13.980
It would've been impossible to see anything.

18:13.980 --> 18:17.270
The culprit's tattoo is in
a hard-to-spot place on his wrist

18:17.270 --> 18:19.870
and it's difficult to make out,

18:19.870 --> 18:23.330
so how did you instantly know it was a bird?

18:25.470 --> 18:26.680
Yamane...

18:26.680 --> 18:28.670
He's wrong! It wasn't me!

18:28.670 --> 18:30.840
Still trying to gloss over everything?

18:31.480 --> 18:33.970
You really can't tell Kawasemi-san, can you?

18:34.920 --> 18:36.740
That you lost your handcuffs.

18:40.650 --> 18:45.160
Earlier, when Yamane-san
lost his button, he panicked

18:45.160 --> 18:47.310
and said, "I found it this time."

18:48.570 --> 18:52.860
In other words, he's already
lost something important to him.

18:53.420 --> 18:57.280
Something which, for example,
might compromise police integrity.

18:58.350 --> 19:00.750
The reason you were so on edge that day

19:00.750 --> 19:03.030
is because you'd lost your cuffs, wasn't it?

19:05.180 --> 19:10.460
That day, when you found the Hand Collector
had killed himself, you had an idea.

19:11.390 --> 19:16.430
To make it seem like he'd fled after you
handcuffed him, you hid his body.

19:16.880 --> 19:19.250
Then you severed his hands.

19:21.230 --> 19:25.390
So when the body was found
handless afterward,

19:25.390 --> 19:30.480
it would look like the Hand Collector
had taken the cuffs along with his hands.

19:31.130 --> 19:33.150
No one would know you'd lost them.

19:33.150 --> 19:34.450
Impossible!

19:34.450 --> 19:36.190
My best subordinate would never—

19:36.190 --> 19:37.600
That's exactly the problem!

19:38.360 --> 19:41.960
It's obvious how much you value Yamane-san.

19:43.050 --> 19:44.940
But the pressure of that...

19:45.390 --> 19:50.590
It meant Yamane-san couldn't allow
himself to be any less than your ideal.

19:59.870 --> 20:01.930
I'm sorry, Kawasemi-san!

20:02.560 --> 20:07.850
I've left a black mark on your career!

20:16.540 --> 20:19.890
The responsibility was
too much for me to bear!

20:19.890 --> 20:22.450
I couldn't meet your expectations!

20:45.100 --> 20:46.160
Yamane.

20:48.720 --> 20:52.010
It will be difficult to reinstate you
as a police officer.

20:54.190 --> 20:55.190
However...

20:56.650 --> 20:58.630
As long as you have the will,

20:59.110 --> 21:01.010
I'll be waiting for my partner to return.

21:22.130 --> 21:26.430
There's no need for both members
of a team to be police officers, is there?

21:27.140 --> 21:30.010
Like how you two solved this mystery.

21:32.910 --> 21:34.920
Don't underestimate my eyes.

21:35.780 --> 21:39.780
Just as I was able to focus on investigating
because Yamane was with me,

21:40.340 --> 21:42.990
this puppet master needs you to harness

21:43.350 --> 21:45.450
his full ability, doesn't he?

21:48.660 --> 21:49.910
Impressive, Eagle Eye—

21:49.910 --> 21:52.620
No, no! That's not the issue here!

21:52.620 --> 21:54.470
This guy makes all kinds of messes,

21:54.470 --> 21:56.820
so I have to keep an eye on him
or he's worthless!

21:56.820 --> 21:59.010
How am I worthless?

21:59.620 --> 22:00.230
Hey, that's right. You didn't try
to pressure the culprit today.

22:00.230 --> 22:02.910
So this<i> is Isshiki Totomaru.
Hey, that's right. You didn't try
to pressure the culprit today.</i>

22:02.910 --> 22:03.230
Hey, that's right. You didn't try
to pressure the culprit today.

22:03.230 --> 22:04.030
He wasn't a murderer.
Yamane-kun didn't kill anyone, right?

22:04.030 --> 22:05.590
You've got a good man there...
He wasn't a murderer.
Yamane-kun didn't kill anyone, right?

22:05.590 --> 22:06.980
He wasn't a murderer.
Yamane-kun didn't kill anyone, right?

22:06.980 --> 22:07.830
Amamiya.
He wasn't a murderer.
Yamane-kun didn't kill anyone, right?

22:07.830 --> 22:09.970
That's how it works?!
